-- EXPECT-ERROR: tuple construction allocates in a `cap no_alloc` module
-- Capabilities widening, Task 4 -- `cap no_alloc` (`lib/refinecheck/no_alloc.ml`),
-- the REJECT side: a non-empty `ETuple` inside a `cap no_alloc` module's
-- function body. `check_expr`'s `ETuple` arm (`no_alloc.ml:20-24`) special-
-- cases the EMPTY tuple `()` as non-allocating (unit carries no heap cell)
-- but raises on any non-empty tuple literal -- `make_pair`'s `(a, b)`
-- return expression allocates a 2-tuple, so `--check` exits 1 with `` tuple
-- construction allocates in a `cap no_alloc` module. ``. See
-- core-march-types.md §2.8.11.
mod NoAllocPair do
  cap no_alloc

  fn make_pair(a : Int, b : Int) : (Int, Int) do
    (a, b)
  end
end
